Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-11-2001||06:50 PM||||josh, you can get the headliner fabric at any fabric store. It comes with the foam on the back. Its only $3.49 a yard here 52'' wide. Dont use the spray can glue, go to Sears or another hardware store and get a pint of Contact cement. It wont fall back down in a week. By the way its called J&S Fabric.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||02-11-2001||07:26 PM||||Mr. Mike's quit carrying carpet <I>etc.</I> about the time I inquired to order mats.  Bummer.  Evidently Mr. Mike's supplier changed their product and he was not pleased with quality.<P>I got headliner and spray glue from Pep Boys.  It was no fun to install because the ceiling board is awkward and delicate.  But 7 months later it still looks good.<BR>||||reg||1
